[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4364270974","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119174#issuecomment-4364270974","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119174","id":4364270974,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBCF9fg","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-02T16:42:57Z","updated_at":"2026-05-02T16:43:33Z","body":"I should have added the 4th condition: the wrapped value needs to be stored as a pointer `T *` within the `template<T>` for this to happen. \r\nIt kind of makes sense where the bug is coming from in that case, whereby:\r\n1. The wrapped object is never explicitly unwrapped (condition 1)\r\n2. No symbols from the class header are used (conditions 2&3)\r\n3. The template doesn't need the full type definition (condition 4)\r\n\r\nThe issue is likely that `include-cleaner` doesn't support operator `->` overloading with child classes in its logic. I might try to fix it on LLVM's repo directly. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4364270974/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4364378370","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119174#issuecomment-4364378370","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119174","id":4364378370,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBCMhAg","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-02T17:44:50Z","updated_at":"2026-05-02T17:44:50Z","body":"Ok, whilst trying to reduce my MRP to its smallest shape for bugfixing, I figured it out: \r\nIt didn't like the `using element_type = T` for some reason...\r\n\r\nBy removing this, I was able to make clangd-tidy work out of the box with the template in all cases except one:\r\nIn [`snapshot_collector.cpp`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/16bb065ac31b79c0ed24b3b944d3b5275123e854/modules/objectdb_profiler/snapshot_collector.cpp#L103), `RequiredParam<Window` is checked for equality against a `Node *` value. For some reason, the equality operator still isn't being parsed for includes properly. I tried overloading it and removing the `using ptr_type = T *`, but nope, still erorring. At this point, this is such a minor edge case (namely, it is only ever used for equality checks in the file where it is included) that I'm not too upset about it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4364378370/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4364411092","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119174#issuecomment-4364411092","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119174","id":4364411092,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBCOg1A","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-0